; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Your First Square
; CATEGORY: Shapes & Polygons
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     square, repeat, procedures, first steps
; SUMMARY:  Draws a square the long way, then the short way with REPEAT, then a row of colored squares.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   The turtle draws three squares. The first is made with eight
;   separate commands, the second with one REPEAT line, and then a
;   new word, SQUARE, is taught to Logo and used to draw a row of
;   squares that get bigger and change color.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Then type your own commands in the command center,
;   for example:  square 120
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * FORWARD and RIGHT move and turn the turtle
;   * REPEAT saves you from typing the same thing again and again
;   * TO ... END teaches Logo a new word (a procedure)
;   * an input like :size lets one procedure draw many sizes
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Change 90 to 120 and 3 in the REPEAT. What shape do you get?
;   * Make the squares in the row grow by 20 instead of 15.
;   * Use SETPENSIZE 5 before drawing to get fat lines.
; ============================================================

; A square has four equal sides and four corners of 90 degrees.
; The turtle turns 90 degrees at every corner, 4 x 90 = 360,
; so it ends up facing the same way it started.
to square :size
  repeat 4 [forward :size right 90]
end

; The long way: every side and every turn written out.
; Reading it aloud helps: walk, turn, walk, turn ...
to longwaysquare
  forward 80 right 90
  forward 80 right 90
  forward 80 right 90
  forward 80 right 90
end

; Jump to a spot without leaving a line behind.
to jumpto :x :y
  penup
  setxy :x :y
  pendown
end

; A row of squares. Each one is 15 steps bigger than the last
; and uses the next color in the palette (colors 1, 2, 3 ...).
to squarerow :count
  repeat :count [
    setpencolor repcount
    square 15 + 15 * repcount
    penup right 90 forward 30 + 15 * repcount left 90 pendown
  ]
end

clearscreen
setpensize 3

; square number one, the long way, in blue
jumpto -300 100
setpencolor 1
longwaysquare

; square number two, the short way, in red
jumpto -150 100
setpencolor 4
repeat 4 [forward 80 right 90]

; square number three, using our new word
jumpto 0 100
setpencolor 13
square 80

; and now a whole row, all built from the same SQUARE
jumpto -280 -220
squarerow 6
hideturtle
